      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fbd23f22-b901-4724-a43b-ab0bef6926d6",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Map – properties\r\n\r\nA `Map` stores **key → value pairs**, like a dictionary: you look up a value by its key (`roll number → name`, `word → count`). It is an **interface** from `java.util`.\r\n\r\n**Properties**\r\n- **Keys are unique**: putting a key that already exists **replaces** its value.\r\n- **Values can repeat**: two keys can have the same value.\r\n- **No index**: you read a value with `get(key)`, not `get(0)`.\r\n- Order depends on the class you pick:\r\n  - `HashMap` – no fixed order (fastest).\r\n  - `LinkedHashMap` – keeps the **insertion order**.\r\n  - `TreeMap` – keeps the keys **sorted**.\r\n- Keys and values must be **objects**: use `Integer`, `Double`… instead of `int`, `double`.\r\n- `HashMap` and `LinkedHashMap` allow one `null` key and many `null` values; `TreeMap` does not allow a `null` key.\r\n- A `Map` is **not** a `Collection`: it has no `add()`, you use `put(key, value)`.\r\n- **Not synchronized** (not thread-safe).",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "fbd23f22-b901-4724-a43b-ab0bef6926d6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "961565e0-32a7-4d1d-a50a-09ad1866bef7",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "//Map\r\n\r\nMap<Integer,String> map = new HashMap<Integer,String>();\r\nmap.put(1,\"One\");\r\nmap.put(2,\"Two\");\r\nmap.put(3,\"Three\");\r\nmap.putIfAbsent(4,\"Four\");\r\nmap.putAll(Map.of(5,\"Five\",6,\"Six\"));\r\n\r\n//map.clear();\r\n\r\nboolean hasKeyThree = map.containsKey(3);\r\nboolean hasValueTwo = map.containsValue(\"fifth\");\r\n\r\nint size = map.size();\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Has key 3: \" + hasKeyThree);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Has value 'Two': \" + hasValueTwo);\r\nSystem.out.println(\"Map size: \" + size);\r\nSystem.out.println(map);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 24,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 24,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Has key 3: true\r\nHas value 'Two': false\r\nMap size: 6\r\n{1=One, 2=Two, 3=Three, 4=Four, 5=Five, 6=Six}\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 24
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fc4f65a1-8fe7-489c-b1e8-f04c830938c2",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "//Syntax\r\n//Map<KeyType, ValueType> variable_name = new HashMap<KeyType, ValueType>();\r\n\r\n//this is to create an empty Map\r\n// Method: new HashMap<>()\r\n// What:   creates an empty map with no fixed order\r\n// Use:    to store key → value pairs when the order does not matter\r\nMap<Integer, String> students = new HashMap<Integer, String>();\r\nSystem.out.println(\"The map is: \" + students);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "fc4f65a1-8fe7-489c-b1e8-f04c830938c2",
        "executionSummary": {
